00:10:12.769 --> 00:10:15.350
What are these heuristics trying to remove?

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:21.710
Let's first have a look what makes most of it.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:32.610
According to The Pile, a data set from E
leutherAI, they calculated 13-grams across

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:37.990
common crawl dumps they used. 13-grams,
you can imagine it's a sliding window.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.669
It always take 13 tokens at once.

00:10:41.049 --> 00:10:46.850
And if you were in last night's talk from
Ting and Leon you know what a token is.

00:10:47.629 --> 00:10:51.230
So it, like, moves one token at a time.

00:10:51.409 --> 00:10:57.750
And the most frequently occurred 13-grams
is dash dash space dash dash for styling.

00:10:58.409 --> 00:11:05.330
It occurred 11 million times. As
well as some boilerplate like this.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.809
"select the forum you want to
visit from the selection below"

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:12.090
It's repeated for 180,000 times.

00:11:14.909 --> 00:11:20.269
So, basically, for texts, they targeted
automatically generated content

00:11:20.269 --> 00:11:26.909
like boilerplate error messages,
like the phrase cookie policies,

00:11:26.909 --> 00:11:32.950
or adding to shopping cart, plus
SEO keywords, or basically anything

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:36.789
that is generated for search engine
rather than for human audience.

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:41.330
And duplicated content, a lot of them.

00:11:41.529 --> 00:11:45.230
Of course, pornographic and otherwise bad stuff.

00:11:45.509 --> 00:11:47.909
This type we will talk in a little bit.

00:11:48.429 --> 00:11:51.090
So, for the first three types, they got pretty

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:54.470
interesting angles to make
those texts pure and average.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:00.129
They tried to remove pages
containing curly brackets because

00:12:00.129 --> 00:12:04.850
they are not used in natural
language but is used a lot in code.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:08.529
And then they calculate the ratio of closed class

00:12:08.529 --> 00:12:16.610
words like "the", "be", "
of", "that", "to", et cetera.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:25.169
Because they are an indicator
of non-human generated content.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:29.190
Or basically, imagine a SEO page
would have very little of them.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:35.409
As well as punctuation marks. They
are the symbol of word composition.

00:12:36.149 --> 00:12:39.710
Too many sentences ending
with ellipses. Not qualified.

00:12:40.809 --> 00:12:43.210
Or sometimes they try to find a reference point.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:48.490
Here, OBELICS from Hugging Face used
OSCAR, a version of cleaned Common Crawl.

00:12:48.889 --> 00:12:52.210
But usually, they use Wikipedia
as a golden reference point.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:56.389
If one word appears there twice,
then it must be a normal word.

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:03.490
And for codes, they try to
remove:I will go through it fast.

00:13:03.929 --> 00:13:08.629
They try to remove documents
with few or a lot of comments.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:11.590
They remove the license
statements in the document.

00:13:12.169 --> 00:13:16.450
They remove super long lines
or if a line is mostly digits.

00:13:16.789 --> 00:13:20.490
They remove repository has no or very few stars.

00:13:21.149 --> 00:13:26.389
And they wanted to remove generated
code. Not necessarily vibe coded code.

00:13:26.769 --> 00:13:33.330
But it could be like a generated diagram
for the architecture of the code or stuff.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:37.710
If you go through some of the data
sets, you'll notice that these

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:42.870
years, almost all the code
subsets are from Stack V1 and V2.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:49.629
And there was a cleaning pipeline
from StarCoder and RedPajama.

00:13:50.509 --> 00:13:58.590
The Stack says that they use only permissive
licensed code from GitHub but I doubt it.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:03.529
Because I found my own repository
there. It was my old personal website.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.549
And I was too lazy to set any license.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.470
So it should be, you know, by default copyrighted

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:13.409
and should not be included in their data sets.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:20.809
For filtering images, the main focus
are the size, resolution, image ratios.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:23.090
Too small is not good. Can be icons and logos.

00:14:23.289 --> 00:14:27.649
Too far away from squares, not good. Can
be banners for ads. Too big is not good.

00:14:27.909 --> 00:14:28.909
It can be [unintelligible].

00:14:29.889 --> 00:14:37.549
And the last category, we will talk
together later with the text part.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:43.149
So, sometimes, apart from the image
size and ratio, amount also matters.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:49.389
OBELICS doesn't include any web page which
has more than 30 images in one page.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:54.789
And some data sets also filter with image URL.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:15:01.629
So, basically, if your image name
contains any words including logo, button,

00:15:02.049 --> 00:15:09.629
icon, plugin, widget, porn, sex, XXX,
in the image, they will get removed.

00:15:10.769 --> 00:15:17.070
Okay. Now, we're finally here for
pornographic and otherwise bad text and image.

00:15:17.509 --> 00:15:21.090
I didn't make this into two
categories, but for some

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:25.549
reason, porns are always separated
from otherwise bad stuff.

00:15:26.289 --> 00:15:30.250
And if you go through several data
